# Benefits of Using AI in Education

Teachers spend a significant portion of their roughly 50-hour workweek on preparation, evaluation, and administrative responsibilities. In fact, less than half of a teacher's time is spent in direct interaction with students.

<div style="width:100%; text-align:center;">

<div style="display:inline-block; border:1px solid #d6d6d6; border-radius:18px; padding:24px 28px;">

<h2 style="margin-top:0; margin-bottom:18px; color:#444;">
Teacher Workday
</h2>

<img src="https://images.code.org/43c45055ef874764a0fdf2a7c1d0387a-Screenshot 2026-02-04 at 2.27.14 PM.png" alt="Pie chart showing 49% of a teacher's time in direct interaction with students." style="width:100%; max-width:700px; display:block; margin:auto; border-radius:12px;">

<div style="margin-top:10px; font-size:14px; color:#666; font-style:italic;">
Image: McKinsey 2020
</div>

</div>
</div>

<br>

For many educators, the greatest benefit of AI is its ability to reduce time spent on routine tasks, creating more time for what matters most: working directly with students.
